 "note": "Two columns joined on each line; I separated them by reading order and the position/date lines under each name. Left column: SUPERINTENDENT OF SCHOOLS (line 2), ASSISTANT SUPERINTENDENT (5), CLERICAL STAFF/Central Office (8) -> central-office; HIGH SCHOOL ADMINISTRATION (20) and CLERICAL STAFF/High School (25) -> high; MIDDLE SCHOOL ADMINISTRATION (36) and CLERICAL STAFF/Middle School (42) -> middle (printed 'Middle School'); ELEMENTARY SCHOOL ADMINISTRATION (49) and CLERICAL STAFF/Elementary School (53) -> passios (bare 'Elementary School'; the Primary School is a separate heading on p120, and Passios is the elementary building in the 1975 and 1981 reports; inference). Right column: GUIDANCE DEPARTMENT (2), GUIDANCE CLERICAL (17), SPECIAL NEEDS DEPARTMENT (22). Guidance/Special Needs roles with a printed grade span: 9-12 -> high, 6-8 -> middle, K-5 / K-12 -> district-wide; Murray (line 49, on leave-of-absence, no position printed) -> unknown. Headings share lines 2, 8, 17, 22(heading only), 36, 42, 49, 53 with entries or continuation lines. Position and (B.date) hire-date lines under names are ignored but role_raw carries the position. Honorifics kept as printed except 'Dr.' kept too. Line 59 page number; line 1 title. 'RESIGNED 9/25/80' (Racine) and 'maternity leave' notes are inline, not a separate list. Names: Hughes on this page is 'Marybarbara T. Hughes'. Integration pass, 31 Oct 2026: school bus contractors, drivers and volunteers moved from entries to ignored (not school staff; every 1971-1980 page treated alike), and `middle` written `turkey-hill` -- the 1972 and 1974 listings print the building as `Turkey Hill Middle School (Grades 5-7)`, the town's one middle school."
